+# Analysis tools this repository installs and runs directly.
+#
+# These replaced Super-Linter (#365), which bundled thirty checks behind one
+# status and one supplier. Each is now taken from its publisher, pinned in
+# scripts/versions.env, and owned by exactly one lane - which is the convention
+# everywhere else here and the thing the aggregate was always the exception to.
+#
+# Being honest about what this section is: the scanners that came before these -
+# TruffleHog, Semgrep, Trivy - are NOT declared anywhere in this file, and
+# neither are the GitHub Actions every workflow uses. #385 covers that gap, and
+# this section is the shape its answer should take, not a complete list of what
